	"title"		"More Nodes/Segments v5.0"
	"description"		"[h1]✨ WHAT'S NEW IN v5.0 (Rebranded to More Nodes/Segments) ✨[/h1]
[list]
[*] [b]Major Release & Official Rebranding:[/b]
[list]
    [*] Rebranded to [b]More Nodes/Segments v5.0[/b]!
    [*] Consolidated 64K network limit expansion (up to 65,024 nodes and segments) with native Apple Silicon & Intel Mac stability.
[/list]
[*] [b]Thread-Safe Save & Quit Armor (from v4.3.48):[/b]
[list]
    [*] Fixed background-thread [i]QuitApplication()[/i] call during save completion, delegating safely to the Main Thread via [i]ThreadHelper.dispatcher.Dispatch[/i]. Completely eliminates off-thread Unity UI [i]NullReferenceException[/i] in Adaptive Roads and rendering engines.
[/list]
[*] [b]Water Transport & Ship Navigation Segregation (v5.0.2 Hotfix):[/b]
[list]
    [*] [b]Clean Route Segregation:[/b] Large ocean ships (cargo and cruise ships) are strictly confined to open-water Ship Paths ([i]Layer.ShipPaths[/i]). Ferry paths, canals, and marina loops are strictly Ferry-only, permanently preventing large ships from entering shallow, narrow ferry routes or getting stuck on tight curves.
    [*] [b]Harbor & Dock Reconnection:[/b] Harbors now connect exclusively to legitimate Ship Paths with zero false snapping to ferry routes.
    [*] [b]Zero Traffic Hooks:[/b] 100% native traffic simulation (strictly zero hooks into vehicle AI, pathfinding, or TM:PE traffic rules).
[/list]
[*] [b]Impatient Commuters Compatibility (v5.0.1 Hotfix):[/b]
[list]
    [*] Added automatic in-memory array expansion (up to 65,536 elements) for [b]Impatient Commuters[/b], completely eliminating simulation thread freeze ([i]IndexOutOfRangeException[/i]) on high-ID public transport stops (> 32,768).
    [*] Strict zero-hook architecture: does not modify or hook into the mod's code, achieving pure memory buffer harmony.
[*] [b]Citizen/Path Units & 81 Tiles 2 Harmonization (v5.0.3 Hotfix):[/b]
[list]
    [*] [b]Universal Dynamic Buffer Guard:[/b] Pre-allocates 1M CitizenUnits and 524K PathUnits before deserialization and preserves savegame metadata override flags bidirectionally, completely resolving [i]IndexOutOfRangeException[/i] in [i]CitizenManager.Data.Deserialize[/i].
    [*] [b]81 Tiles 2 Auto-Harmonization:[/b] Deferred early [i]NetManager.instance[/i] access and auto-expanded [i]NetManager.m_tileNodesCount[/i] to 3402, completely removing the 1050 size mismatch error.
    [*] [b]Level Reload State Sanitizer:[/b] Clears pending TM:PE serialization buffers and runs strategic garbage collection on level unload, eliminating reload blue screens / freezes on cities > 34K nodes.
    [*] [b]Universal Mod Harmonizer:[/b] Added dynamic memory harmonization for present and future community mods.
[*] [b]UTF-16 Sanitizer & Orphan Vehicle Cleaner (v5.0.4 Hotfix):[/b]
[list]
    [*] [b]Universal UTF-16 Sanitizer Armor:[/b] Automatically repairs corrupted and orphaned UTF-16 surrogate pairs in strings deserialized from savegames ([i]DataSerializer.ReadUniqueString[/i]) and passed to Unity logging ([i]DebugLogHandler.LogFormat[/i]). Completely resolves [i]System.ArgumentException: invalid utf-16 sequence (missing surrogate head)[/i] in [i]PrefabCollection<VehicleInfo>.BindPrefabs[/i] and [i]Loading Screen Mod[/i].
    [*] [b]Orphan Vehicle Cleaner:[/b] Automatically identifies and safely releases orphaned vehicles and parked vehicles whose custom prefabs were deleted or corrupted ([i]VehicleManager.Data.AfterDeserialize[/i]), permanently eliminating downstream [i]NullReferenceException[/i] in [b]Transport Lines Manager (TLM)[/b] and transit simulation threads.
[/list]
[/list]

[hr][/hr]

[h1]MORE NODES/SEGMENTS v5.0[/h1]
[b]The Definitive 64K Network Limit Breaker for Cities: Skylines[/b]
[i]Fully rewritten, optimized, and stabilized by NgocDuy[/i]

[hr][/hr]

[h1]WHAT IS THIS MOD?[/h1]
Have you ever hit the infamous [b]'Cannot create more objects of this type'[/b] limit while building your dream metropolis?
Vanilla Cities: Skylines caps your road and transit networks at ~32,000 nodes and segments.

[b]More Nodes/Segments v5.0[/b] safely expands your game internal network limits to [b]65,536 (64K) Nodes and Segments[/b] - giving you double the building freedom!

Unlike unstable legacy experimental versions that caused fatal crashes and corrupted traffic, [b]More Nodes/Segments[/b] is engineered from the ground up for [b]maximum stability, accurate traffic simulation, and zero data loss.[/b]

[hr][/hr]

[h1]KEY ADVANTAGES & SUPERIOR FEATURES[/h1]
[list]
[*] [b]64K Expanded Capacity:[/b] Doubles the maximum network node and segment limits (up to 65,536) and lanes up to 524,288. Build massive regional transit grids, hyper-detailed highway interchanges, and expansive subway networks without restriction.
[*] [b]Full Road & Building Placement Guarantee:[/b] Solved engine-level ToolController collision bitmask limits (65,536 bits), allowing smooth placement of roads, bridges, tunnels, intersections, and buildings without tool lockups.
[*] [b]Native Apple Silicon & Intel Mac Stability:[/b] Fixed deep engine crash loops, memory boundary overflows, and native crashes that plagued previous limit mods on macOS (M1/M2/M3/M4 & Intel) and Windows.
[*] [b]Complete TM:PE Compatibility:[/b]
[list]
    [*] Timed Traffic Lights (TTL) are 100% operational on expanded nodes (> 32,768).
    [*] Custom lane connections, lane arrows, speed limits, and priority rules are fully respected.
    [*] Node data and timed phases persist cleanly through save/load cycles without missing references.
[/list]
[*] [b]Accurate Traffic Flow & Real-Time Heatmaps:[/b] Full traffic flow color refresh across all extended segments without frozen vehicles or phantom deadlocks.
[*] [b]Safe Persistence Guarantee:[/b] Implements clean savegame serialization to ensure custom traffic setups and extended networks reload perfectly.
[*] [b]Deep Mod Ecosystem Compatibility:[/b] Seamless integration with Adaptive Roads, Network Skins, Node Controller Renewal, Move It, IMT, Network Multitool, Network Anarchy, Picker, Find It, Impatient Commuters, etc.
[/list]

[hr][/hr]

[h1]COMPATIBILITY[/h1]
Tested and fully compatible with the standard modern modding ecosystem:
[list]
[*] [b]Harmony 2.2+[/b] (Required dependency)
[*] [b]TM:PE (Traffic Manager: President Edition)[/b] (STABLE & LABS)
[*] [b]Network Anarchy[/b]
[*] [b]Adaptive Roads (ADR)[/b]
[*] [b]Network Skins 2[/b]
[*] [b]Node Controller Renewal[/b]
[*] [b]Intersection Marking Tool (IMT)[/b]
[*] [b]Network Multitool[/b]
[*] [b]Move It[/b]
[*] [b]Picker[/b]
[*] [b]Find It 2[/b]
[*] [b]81 Tiles 2[/b]
[*] [b]Advanced Road Tools[/b]
[*] [b]Improved Public Transport 2 & 3[/b]
[*] [b]Advanced Vehicle Options[/b]
[*] [b]More CitizenUnits & More PathUnits[/b] (Universal Dynamic Buffer Guard)
[*] [b]Universal Mod Harmonizer[/b] (Zero-conflict compatibility for community mods)
[*] [b]Impatient Commuters[/b] (Auto-expanded to 65K stop nodes)
[/list]

[hr][/hr]

[h1]REQUIREMENTS[/h1]
[list]
[*] [url=https://steamcommunity.com/workshop/filedetails/?id=2040656402]Harmony 2.2.2-0 (CitiesHarmony)[/url]
[/list]

[hr][/hr]

[h1]BEST PRACTICES & RECOMMENDATIONS[/h1]
[list]
[*] [b]Backup Your Saves:[/b] As with any mod altering foundational game limits, always keep regular backup copies of your favorite cities.
[*] [b]Persistent Saves:[/b] Once a city exceeds vanilla network limits (> 32,768 nodes/segments), this mod must remain enabled to load and manage those extended networks properly.
[/list]

[hr][/hr]
[i]Developed with precision and care for the Cities: Skylines community by NgocDuy.[/i]"
	"changenote"		"v5.0.6 - Corrupted Save Immunity & Universal Game Loading Armor: Added GameLoadingArmor defending against save corruption and mod crashes (UnlockManager scenario condition overflow guard, RadioPanel null station guard, MessageManager chirper bounds & recovery guard, TransportLinesManager missing prefab vehicle removal guard, and crash-proof native logging P/Invoke protection); 100% preservation of network limit logic and zero loading screen deadlocks."
